1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,400
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,520
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:07,800
This is my brother George.
[GRUNTS]

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,320
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:13,280
And this is Daddy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,760
Peppa Pig.
[GRUNTS]

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,599
[♪♪♪]

8
00:00:17,599 --> 00:00:18,840
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

9
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,480
[♪♪♪]

10
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,320
NARRATOR: Every morning, Peppa
and George brush their teeth.

11
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:28,000
[SCRUBBING, BUBBLES POP]

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,840
NARRATOR:
Today, Peppa and George
are going to the dentist.

13
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:32,640
[SNORTS]
Peppa! George!

14
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,120
Are you ready to go
for your checkup?

15
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:36,640
[GRUNTS]
I'm too busy
for a checkup.

16
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:39,360
I'm having a tea party
with Teddy.

17
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,960
[IMITATES TEDDY]
Yes, we're very busy.

18
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:44,440
We all need checkups.
To make sure our teeth

19
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,839
are clean
and healthy.

20
00:00:45,839 --> 00:00:47,320
Okay, Daddy.

21
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:51,199
[GRUNTS]
George, are your teeth
clean like mine?

22
00:00:51,199 --> 00:00:53,919
NARRATOR:
It is George's first visit
to the dentist.

23
00:00:53,919 --> 00:00:55,800
You both have
lovely, clean teeth.

24
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,160
I'm sure the dentist
will be very happy.

25
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:59,239
[GIGGLING]

26
00:00:59,239 --> 00:01:00,559
[♪♪♪]

27
00:01:00,559 --> 00:01:02,199
[CAR HORN HONKING]

28
00:01:02,199 --> 00:01:04,519
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are at the dentist's,

29
00:01:04,519 --> 00:01:06,240
waiting for their checkup.

30
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,360
[CLOCK TICKING]

31
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:11,240
[YAWNS]
Waiting is boring.

32
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:13,560
This magazine's
very interesting.

33
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:16,240
[SNORTS]
It's all about potatoes.

34
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:19,200
[YAWNING]

35
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,960
Peppa? George? The dentist
will see you now.

36
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:25,399
Hooray!
[GIGGLES]

37
00:01:25,399 --> 00:01:28,399
NARRATOR:
This is Dr. Elephant,
the dentist.

38
00:01:28,399 --> 00:01:31,479
Hello, Peppa. Have you been
brushing your teeth?

39
00:01:31,479 --> 00:01:33,039
Yes, Dr. Elephant!

40
00:01:33,039 --> 00:01:35,520
Good.
Now, who's first?

41
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:38,399
I'm first, because
I'm a big girl.

42
00:01:38,399 --> 00:01:40,640
[SNORTS]
Watch me, George!

43
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,800
Sit in the chair,
please.

44
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,920
[GIGGLING]
Hold tight.

45
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,920
[CLICKS LEVER, CHAIR HUMMING]
Wee!

46
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,399
[GIGGLES]

47
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:50,039
Open wide, please.
Ah.

48
00:01:50,039 --> 00:01:53,640
Wider, please.
Ah!

49
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,960
Now.
Let's take a look.

50
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,039
NARRATOR: Dr. Elephant
uses a little mirror

51
00:01:58,039 --> 00:01:59,800
to look at Peppa's teeth.

52
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,960
I hope you haven't been eating
too many sweeties, Peppa!

53
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:05,399
[GARBLED TALKING]

54
00:02:05,399 --> 00:02:08,799
NARRATOR:
It is quite difficult to speak
when your mouth is wide open.

55
00:02:08,799 --> 00:02:11,600
[GARBLED TALKING]
[CHUCKLES]

56
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:16,600
There! All done!
What lovely clean teeth!

57
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:18,200
She takes after me.

58
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,040
[ALL CHUCKLE]

59
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:23,200
[GRUNTS]
Can I have the special
pink drink now?

60
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,079
Yes! But don't drink it,
Peppa, spit it out.

61
00:02:27,079 --> 00:02:28,799
[GARGLING]

62
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,880
[ALL GIGGLE]

63
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,799
[SNORTS]
George, now it's your turn.

64
00:02:33,799 --> 00:02:35,560
No.

65
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,760
NARRATOR: George does not
want it to be his turn.

66
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,200
Maybe you can hold
Mr. Dinosaur,

67
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,680
while the dentist
looks at your teeth.

68
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:46,359
[GIGGLES]
Grrrr! Dine-Saw!

69
00:02:46,359 --> 00:02:49,720
Heh-heh-heh. Very pleased
to meet you, Mr. Dinosaur.

70
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:53,720
It's not a real dinosaur.
It's made of plastic.

71
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,440
[LAUGHS]
Hold tight.

72
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,880
[CLICKS LEVER, CHAIR HUMMING]

73
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:00,280
You're doing
very well, George.

74
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:03,400
Now, can you
show me your teeth?

75
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:06,160
NARRATOR: George does not want
to show the dentist his teeth.

76
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:10,079
George, open wide.
Like this...

77
00:03:10,079 --> 00:03:11,600
Ah!

78
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:14,760
[SNICKERS]
Ah!

79
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:18,320
Ah, there they are.

80
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:19,600
All done.

81
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:23,000
You have very strong,
clean teeth, George.

82
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,160
Are they as lovely as mine,
Dr. Elephant?

83
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:28,320
Ah.
Yes.

84
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,519
[ALL LAUGHING]

85
00:03:29,519 --> 00:03:31,239
[GIGGLES, GRUNTS]

86
00:03:31,239 --> 00:03:34,079
NARRATOR: George is very proud
to have clean teeth.

87
00:03:34,079 --> 00:03:37,040
George! Don't forget
the pink drink.

88
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,679
[GARGLING]

89
00:03:42,399 --> 00:03:44,399
Oh, but wait.
What's this?

90
00:03:44,399 --> 00:03:46,079
What's wrong,
Dr. Elephant?

91
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:47,560
George has clean teeth,

92
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,399
but this young dinosaur's
teeth are very dirty.

93
00:03:50,399 --> 00:03:55,600
Oh no! Dr. Elephant is very
cross with Mr. Dinosaur.

94
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,119
Ha! Ha! Not at all, Peppa.

95
00:03:57,119 --> 00:03:59,679
It's my job to
make teeth clean.

96
00:03:59,679 --> 00:04:01,280
The water jet, please,
Miss Rabbit.

97
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,280
[♪♪♪]

98
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:06,600
NARRATOR: The dentist uses water
to clean Mr. Dinosaur's teeth.

99
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,560
The polisher, please,
Miss Rabbit.

100
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,399
[♪♪♪]

101
00:04:10,399 --> 00:04:12,760
This will be a bit noisy.
[POLISHER CLICKING]

102
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:15,799
NARRATOR: Dr. Elephant polishes
Mr. Dinosaur's teeth.

103
00:04:15,799 --> 00:04:17,200
Pink! Pink!

104
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,599
That's right, George.

105
00:04:18,599 --> 00:04:21,839
Mr. Dinosaur needs some special
pink drink.

106
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:27,479
[♪♪♪]

107
00:04:27,479 --> 00:04:31,599
Gosh. What shiny teeth
you have, Mr. Dinosaur.

108
00:04:31,599 --> 00:04:34,039
Grrrrr.

109
00:04:34,039 --> 00:04:35,320
[GIGGLES]

110
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:39,760
Dine-Saw.
Eek. Too scary.

111
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:41,919
NARRATOR:
George loves Mr. Dinosaur.

112
00:04:41,919 --> 00:04:44,159
Especially now he has nice,
clean teeth.

113
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:45,880
[ALL LAUGH]

114
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:48,080
[KIDS LAUGHING]

115
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,320
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

116
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:53,919
NARRATOR: Peppa and her friends
are going on a school bus trip.

117
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:56,680
Children. Children.

118
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:58,560
Attention, please.

119
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:01,080
Let's check that
you're all here.

120
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,680
Peppa and George.

121
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,479
Here.
[GRUNTS]

122
00:05:05,479 --> 00:05:07,360
Rebecca and
Richard Rabbit?

123
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:10,240
Here. Squeak.
Squeak, squeak.

124
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,840
Suzy sheep?
Here. Baa...

125
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:15,520
Zoe Zebra?
Here.

126
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,080
Danny Dog?
Here. Ruff, ruff.

127
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,360
Emily Elephant?
Here.

128
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,919
[TRUMPETS]

129
00:05:21,919 --> 00:05:23,320
[GIGGLES]

130
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,120
Pedro Pony?

131
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,960
NARRATOR:
Pedro Pony is not here.

132
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:30,800
[BOTH PANTING]
Sorry we're late.

133
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:34,240
Pedro. You almost
missed the school trip.

134
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,039
Sorry, Madame Gazelle.

135
00:05:36,039 --> 00:05:38,359
Never mind, you're
just in time.

136
00:05:38,359 --> 00:05:40,479
[RINGS BELL]
All aboard.

137
00:05:40,479 --> 00:05:42,880
Neigh.
[GIGGLES]

138
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,680
NARRATOR:
Miss Rabbit is the bus driver.

139
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,840
[RINGS BELL]
Full steam ahead.

140
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:49,400
ALL:
See you later.

141
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:51,560
[KIDS GIGGLING]

142
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,080
[ALL CONTINUE GIGGLING]

143
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:58,200
Children.
Attention, please.

144
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:01,840
Today, we are going on
a trip to the mountains.

145
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:03,479
ALL:
Hooray!

146
00:06:03,479 --> 00:06:05,599
MADAME GAZELLE:
Have you all got
your lunchboxes?

147
00:06:05,599 --> 00:06:07,560
ALL:
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

148
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:11,000
Madame Gazelle, please
can we eat our lunch now?

149
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,400
Peppa. We'll eat lunch when
we arrive in the mountains.

150
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:18,719
Peppa? What have you got
in your lunchbox?

151
00:06:18,719 --> 00:06:21,840
A red apple.
I've got a green apple.

152
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,359
Let's swap.
Okay.

153
00:06:24,359 --> 00:06:26,680
[BOTH CHUCKLE, CRUNCH]

154
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,320
MADAME GAZELLE:
Peppa. Suzy.

155
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,680
What are you doing?

156
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,440
Suzy told me to open
my lunchbox.

157
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:34,960
Peppa told me
to swap our apples.

158
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:36,520
Ho, ho. That's fine.

159
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:39,240
But please, save some
food for the picnic.

160
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,159
BOTH:
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

161
00:06:41,159 --> 00:06:43,400
[KIDS LAUGHING]

162
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,440
NARRATOR: The bus has arrived
at the foot of the mountains.

163
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,880
[BUS GEARS GRINDING]

164
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,039
NARRATOR:
The mountain road
is very steep.

165
00:06:50,039 --> 00:06:52,560
Come on, bus.
You can make it.

166
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:55,599
[GEARS GRIND]
ALL: Come on, bus.

167
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,200
KIDS:
Hooray!

168
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:00,120
[GIGGLING]

169
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,960
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends are
at the top of the mountain.

170
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:05,680
[♪♪♪]

171
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:08,919
Look at the view.
Wow.

172
00:07:08,919 --> 00:07:11,159
[ECHOES]
Wow.

173
00:07:11,159 --> 00:07:13,039
Who said that?

174
00:07:13,039 --> 00:07:14,919
It's your echo.

175
00:07:14,919 --> 00:07:16,520
What's my echo?

176
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,760
An echo is the sound you hear

177
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:21,280
when you speak loudly
in the mountains.

178
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,640
Like this.

179
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,919
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo.

180
00:07:24,919 --> 00:07:28,680
[ECHOES]
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo.
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo.

181
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,000
[GIGGLES, CLEARS THROAT]

182
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,960
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo.

183
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:36,320
[ECHOES]
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo.
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo.

184
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,320
[ALL CHUCKLE]

185
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:46,280
[KIDS SHOUTING]
[ECHOING]

186
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:48,680
[ALL GIGGLE]
NARRATOR: Echoes are fun.

187
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,440
Time for our picnic.

188
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:55,239
NARRATOR: Peppa loves picnics.
Everyone loves picnics.

189
00:07:55,239 --> 00:07:57,159
[GRUNTS]
Where are the ducks?

190
00:07:57,159 --> 00:08:00,159
They always turn up
when we have picnics.

191
00:08:00,159 --> 00:08:04,039
Silly Peppa. Ducks don't
live on top of mountains.

192
00:08:04,039 --> 00:08:05,560
[DUCK QUACKS]
Oh.

193
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,280
Quack.
Quack.
Quack.

194
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:08,640
Hello, Mrs. Duck.

195
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:11,320
Would you like some bread?
[QUACKS]

196
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,400
NARRATOR: The ducks
are very lucky today.

197
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,919
There is lots of bread.

198
00:08:15,919 --> 00:08:17,479
[ALL MUNCHING]

199
00:08:17,479 --> 00:08:19,560
NARRATOR: The ducks are eating
too quickly.

200
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,080
[HICCUPS]
Goodness me.

201
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,239
[HICCUPS]
[BURPS]

202
00:08:23,239 --> 00:08:24,679
[KIDS LAUGH]

203
00:08:24,679 --> 00:08:27,320
[BUS BELL RINGS]
MISS RABBIT: Home time.

204
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:28,719
All aboard.

205
00:08:28,719 --> 00:08:30,239
NARRATOR:
It's time to go home.

206
00:08:30,239 --> 00:08:31,520
[RINGS BELL]

207
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,480
NARRATOR:
Everybody has had a great time.

208
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:37,240
[KIDS LAUGHING]

209
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:39,280
Let's all sing a song.

210
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,919
Can we have
"The Bing Bong Song", please?

211
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:44,760
Ho, ho.
KIDS: Please, Madame Gazelle,

212
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,800
sing "The Bing Bong Song".

213
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:48,760
All right.

214
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,680
♪ Ooh ♪

215
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:54,199
♪ We're playing our tune and
We're singing our song ♪

216
00:08:54,199 --> 00:08:58,280
♪ With a bing and a bong
And a bing ♪

217
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:01,760
♪ Bong bing boo
Bing bong bing ♪

218
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:05,600
♪ Bing bong
Bingley bungley booooo ♪

219
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:08,840
♪ Bong bing boo
Bing bong bing ♪

220
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:12,240
♪ Bing bong
Bingley bungley booooo. ♪

221
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:15,800
[KIDS LAUGH]
[MADAME GAZELLE PLAYS GUITAR]

222
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,000
[♪♪♪]

223
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,560
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

224
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,839
NARRATOR:
It is the end of
another lovely day.

225
00:09:22,839 --> 00:09:24,680
[KIDS GIGGLING]

226
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:27,280
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are playing with their friends

227
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,920
Rebecca and Richard Rabbit.

228
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,839
Home time,
my little bunnies.

229
00:09:30,839 --> 00:09:33,439
Oh, but we want to
play some more, Mommy.

230
00:09:33,439 --> 00:09:34,800
Maybe tomorrow.

231
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,480
Can Peppa and George
come to our house tomorrow?

232
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,520
Yes.
GIRLS: Hooray!

233
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,800
[GIGGLING]

234
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:44,280
[CRYING]

235
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,079
Why is Richard crying?

236
00:09:46,079 --> 00:09:48,959
He's a bit scared of
going down stairs.

237
00:09:48,959 --> 00:09:50,120
Why?

238
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:52,360
We don't have
stairs in our home.

239
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,240
What? No stairs?

240
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:57,680
That's right. You'll see
tomorrow. Bye bye.

241
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,160
Bye bye.
[SNORTS]

242
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,600
[LAUGHING]
[ENGINE STARTS, HONKS HORN]

243
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,360
[ROOSTER CROWS]

244
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:07,400
NARRATOR: It is morning,
and Peppa and George

245
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,920
are going to Rebecca Rabbit's
house today.

246
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:13,520
[GRUNTS]
Mommy Pig can drive and
I'll do the map reading.

247
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,199
MOMMY PIG:
Are you sure, Daddy Pig?

248
00:10:15,199 --> 00:10:17,760
We always get lost when
you do the map reading.

249
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:20,280
Ha, ha.
We won't get lost.

250
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,760
Okay. Is everybody ready?
[STARTS ENGINE]

251
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,240
Yes, Mommy Pig.
[GEORGE GRUNTS]

252
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:27,240
Then let's go.
[HONKS HORN]

253
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,680
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are very excited,

254
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:32,520
they have never been to
Rebecca Rabbit's house before.

255
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:35,160
[GRUNTS]
Daddy, are we
nearly there?

256
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:38,839
The map says Rebecca's house
is on the next hill.

257
00:10:38,839 --> 00:10:41,079
[♪♪♪]

258
00:10:41,079 --> 00:10:45,319
I don't understand. This should
be where Rebecca Rabbit lives.

259
00:10:45,319 --> 00:10:49,240
We must be lost. There's just
this garden of carrots.

260
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:52,199
NARRATOR: Where can
Rebecca Rabbit's house be?

261
00:10:52,199 --> 00:10:55,520
Squeak. Hello, everyone.
[SQUEAKS]

262
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:57,520
[CHUCKLING]
Rebecca.

263
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,560
Do you want to play
in my bedroom?

264
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:02,719
[GRUNTS]
Your bedroom?
But where is your house?

265
00:11:02,719 --> 00:11:05,560
NARRATOR: Peppa cannot see
Rebecca's house anywhere.

266
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:08,839
This hill is our house.
It's called a burrow.

267
00:11:08,839 --> 00:11:11,199
BOTH: Ooh.
I'll show you.

268
00:11:11,199 --> 00:11:12,760
DADDY PIG:
See you later.

269
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:15,079
See you later.
[STARTS ENGINE, HONKS HORN]

270
00:11:15,079 --> 00:11:16,719
Come in.

271
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:21,560
We don't have stairs,
we have tunnels.

272
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,360
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE:
Wow.

273
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:26,240
NARRATOR: Rebecca's house is
a bit different to Peppa's.

274
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,520
This is our bedroom.

275
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:30,120
Wow.

276
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:35,120
You have a bed, and a window,
and a toybox just like us.

277
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:37,240
Of course.
[CHUCKLES]

278
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:41,319
I like your house.
I wish I was a rabbit.

279
00:11:41,319 --> 00:11:45,160
I know. Shall I teach you
both how to be rabbits?

280
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,160
Yes, please.
[SNORTS]

281
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,719
First, you have to twitch
your nose and squeak.

282
00:11:50,719 --> 00:11:53,680
Like this.
[SQUEAKS]

283
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:56,680
[BOTH SQUEAK]

284
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,120
[BOTH GIGGLE]

285
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:01,800
Very good, Peppa Rabbit
and George Rabbit.

286
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:05,680
NARRATOR:
Peppa likes being a rabbit.
George likes being a rabbit.

287
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,719
Rabbits like carrots.

288
00:12:07,719 --> 00:12:10,600
[MUNCHES]
Delicious.

289
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,920
[CRUNCHING]
Delicious.

290
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:16,240
Yuck.

291
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,480
NARRATOR:
George does not like carrots.

292
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:20,600
He won't even
try them.

293
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,760
Oh well,
more for us then.

294
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:24,000
[CRUNCHING]
[GIGGLING]

295
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,079
Rebecca, what else
do rabbits like?

296
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:28,959
Rabbits like hopping.

297
00:12:28,959 --> 00:12:31,480
Come outside, I'll show you.

298
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:33,959
[ALL LAUGHING]

299
00:12:36,439 --> 00:12:38,920
Let's hop.
[SQUEAKS]

300
00:12:40,599 --> 00:12:42,160
NARRATOR:
Rabbits like hopping.

301
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,400
[ALL SQUEAK]

302
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,439
You're very
good rabbits.

303
00:12:46,439 --> 00:12:51,520
Lunch time, children.
[KIDS GIGGLE]

304
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:56,120
NARRATOR:
Mommy and Daddy Rabbit
have prepared lunch.

305
00:12:56,120 --> 00:13:00,360
[SQUEAKS]
Rebecca has taught us
how to be rabbits.

306
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,680
[BOTH SQUEAK]

307
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:04,319
Ho, ho.
You'll enjoy lunch then,

308
00:13:04,319 --> 00:13:06,959
it's our favorite. Carrots.

309
00:13:06,959 --> 00:13:08,439
Delicious.

310
00:13:08,439 --> 00:13:10,920
Delicious.
Yuck.

311
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:13,760
George will not
eat carrots.

312
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:17,400
Oh dear, George,
I thought you were a rabbit.

313
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:19,599
Rabbits love carrots.

314
00:13:19,599 --> 00:13:22,120
[SQUEAKS, CRUNCHES]

315
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:24,599
Mm.
[MUNCHING]

316
00:13:24,599 --> 00:13:28,560
Wow. George is eating a carrot.
[LAUGHS]

317
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:32,920
And this is our favorite cake.
Carrot cake.

318
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,160
[KIDS]
Hooray!

319
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:36,760
Mm... car-rot cake.

320
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:40,520
[LAUGHS]
George is a proper rabbit now.

321
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:41,800
[SQUEAKS]

322
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:46,240
[ALL GUFFAW]

323
00:13:48,719 --> 00:13:50,719
[♪♪♪]

324
00:13:50,719 --> 00:13:52,800
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

325
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:54,439
NARRATOR:
Today, Peppa and her family

326
00:13:54,439 --> 00:13:56,319
are driving out
to the countryside.

327
00:13:56,319 --> 00:13:59,120
Daddy, what will we see
in the countryside?

328
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:03,000
[GRUNTS]
We'll see birds and trees
and flowers and bees.

329
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,520
[GIGGLES]
Dine-Saw.
No, George.

330
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:09,599
I don't think we'll see
any dinosaurs.

331
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:11,400
[ALL LAUGH]

332
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,880
NARRATOR: This is the start
of the nature trail.

333
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:16,839
We're here.
Hooray.

334
00:14:16,839 --> 00:14:19,479
Daddy Pig, don't
forget the picnic.

335
00:14:19,479 --> 00:14:22,360
Ho, ho.
As if I would.

336
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:25,280
Daddy, how do we know
which way to go?

337
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:29,160
Easy. The map says...
there should be a sign

338
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:32,240
showing the start of
the nature trail here.

339
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,640
Well done, Daddy Pig.
[KIDS GIGGLE]

340
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:39,319
NARRATOR: Oh dear, Daddy Pig
has forgotten the picnic.

341
00:14:41,959 --> 00:14:44,760
Peppa, what interesting
things can you see?

342
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:50,120
Just trees and trees
and more boring trees.

343
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:53,280
Ha-ha-ha, Peppa, you're
not looking hard enough.

344
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,880
All right.

345
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:59,160
I'll look really hard
and I still won't see anything.

346
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:00,719
Oh. What's that?

347
00:15:00,719 --> 00:15:02,760
NARRATOR:
Peppa has found
some footprints.

348
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:06,199
Whose footprints are these?
Dine-Saw.

349
00:15:06,199 --> 00:15:10,479
Oh George, they're not
dinosaur footprints.

350
00:15:10,479 --> 00:15:13,599
Let's follow the footprints
and see who made them.

351
00:15:13,599 --> 00:15:15,400
Yes.
[GRUNTS]

352
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:19,920
Shh. We have to be very quiet
so we don't scare anything away.

353
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:23,160
Yes, Mommy.
George. Shh.

354
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,079
[GIGGLES]
Shh.

355
00:15:25,079 --> 00:15:27,839
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are following the footprints.

356
00:15:27,839 --> 00:15:29,360
Look.

357
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:32,199
MOMMY PIG:
The footprints were made
by a little bird.

358
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:35,319
She's flown into a tree.

359
00:15:35,319 --> 00:15:36,800
Where?
Here, Peppa.

360
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,520
Look through
the binoculars.

361
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,880
NARRATOR: The binoculars make
everything look bigger.

362
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:45,199
PEPPA:
I can see one, two,
three baby birds.

363
00:15:45,199 --> 00:15:49,040
Aw, I wonder what
they're eating.

364
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:52,839
Ew!
They're eating worms!

365
00:15:52,839 --> 00:15:56,640
That's disgusting!
[LAUGHING]

366
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:58,160
[GRUNTS]

367
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:00,280
NARRATOR: George has found
more footprints.

368
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:03,000
Ooh.
What little footprints.

369
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,560
DADDY PIG:
The footprint are
being made by ants.

370
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:09,120
They're collecting
leaves to eat.

371
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:11,400
Are they going to have
salad for lunch?

372
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,760
[LAUGHING]
Yes.

373
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:15,319
Talking of lunch,
let's have our picnic.

374
00:16:15,319 --> 00:16:17,040
Oh, the picnic!

375
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:20,560
Daddy Pig. You've left the
picnic in the car, haven't you?

376
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,719
Uh, yes...

377
00:16:22,719 --> 00:16:26,479
but it's not a problem, we'll
just go back to the car to eat.

378
00:16:26,479 --> 00:16:28,199
But which way is the car?

379
00:16:28,199 --> 00:16:30,520
My map will show us.
[GRUNTS]

380
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,920
This way. Oof.

381
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:34,400
Who put that tree there?

382
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,079
It's not on the map.

383
00:16:36,079 --> 00:16:39,000
Oh, Daddy Pig.
We're lost, aren't we?

384
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Uh... yes.

385
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,120
[SNORTS]
How are we going to find
our little car?

386
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,760
[GRUNTS]

387
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,800
NARRATOR: George has found
more footprints.

388
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:51,920
Ooh, what big footprints.
Dine-saw.

389
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,479
Very interesting.

390
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:58,599
What? Has George found some
real dinosaur footprints?

391
00:16:58,599 --> 00:17:02,280
No, these are
our footprints.

392
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,440
And, if we follow
our footprints,

393
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,599
we'll find the way
back to our car.

394
00:17:06,599 --> 00:17:09,520
And our picnic.
ALL: Hooray!

395
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:11,359
[GRUNTS, GIGGLES]

396
00:17:11,359 --> 00:17:14,720
DADDY PIG:
Ha, ha. Nothing can stop us
finding our car now.

397
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:20,760
We're home and dry.
Oh, I wasn't expecting that.

398
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,040
Luckily, I remembered
the umbrella.

399
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:27,280
NARRATOR: The rain is washing
the footprints away.

400
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,480
How are we going to
find the car now?

401
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,159
And our picnic.

402
00:17:31,159 --> 00:17:32,520
[QUACKING]

403
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:33,960
It's the ducks.

404
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:36,919
They always turn up
at picnics.

405
00:17:36,919 --> 00:17:40,440
Sorry, Mrs. Duck, we haven't
got a picnic this time.

406
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,879
We can't find it.
[QUACKS]

407
00:17:42,879 --> 00:17:47,720
I know. Mrs. Duck, can you help
us find our picnic please?

408
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:50,480
[QUACKING]
[GIGGLES]

409
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,360
[♪♪♪]

410
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:54,440
We're here.
ALL: Hooray.

411
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:56,280
Thank you,
Mrs. Duck.

412
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:59,040
[QUACKS]
[LAUGHS]

413
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:01,399
[ALL MUNCHING]

414
00:18:01,399 --> 00:18:03,680
I love nature trails.

415
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:06,760
Yes, and I love picnics.

416
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,040
And the ducks
love picnics.

417
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,879
And the little birds
love picnics.

418
00:18:10,879 --> 00:18:12,919
DADDY PIG:
And the ants love picnics.

419
00:18:12,919 --> 00:18:15,680
Everybody loves picnics.

420
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:18,720
[ALL LAUGH]

421
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,280
[♪♪♪]

422
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:21,360
[GIGGLING, SNORTING]

423
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,840
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

424
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:25,760
[GRUNTING, GIGGLING]

425
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:28,840
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

426
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:29,919
[SNORTING, LAUGHING]

427
00:18:29,919 --> 00:18:31,560
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

428
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:33,360
[SNORTING]

